    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.8"/>
    <code code="51848-0" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation note"/>
    <title>Assessment</title>
    <text><list><item>Cough for about three months, blood-streaked sputum for two weeks, night sweats, and weight loss of about 6 kg in a man of 28, with a right upper lobe cavity on chest X-ray and CT: suspected pulmonary tuberculosis; home airborne isolation and three sputum samples for acid-fast smear, nucleic acid amplification, and culture: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Moderate protein-calorie malnutrition: BMI 16.8, about 11 percent weight loss in three months, and albumin 3.2 g/dL: active, confirmed [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Infectious diseases consultation to confirm the diagnosis, choose between the six-month and four-month regimens, plan monitoring and his return to teaching, and address cystic fibrosis and alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency as explanations for his lifelong chest illness. Guideline: Official American Thoracic Society/Centers for Disease Control and Prevention/Infectious Diseases Society of America Clinical Practice Guidelines: Treatment of Drug-Susceptible Tuberculosis (2016); Interim Guidance: 4-Month Rifapentine-Moxifloxacin Regimen for the Treatment of Drug-Susceptible Pulmonary Tuberculosis - United States, 2022 (2022) [S]</item><item>Diagnosis: three sputum samples at least eight hours apart, one early in the morning, for acid-fast smear, nucleic acid amplification with rifampin resistance, culture, molecular testing for isoniazid and fluoroquinolone resistance, and phenotypic susceptibility; an interferon-gamma release assay; HIV, hepatitis B, and hepatitis C tests; and baseline blood count, liver and kidney tests, potassium, calcium, and magnesium. Guideline: Official American Thoracic Society/Centers for Disease Control and Prevention/Infectious Diseases Society of America Clinical Practice Guidelines: Treatment of Drug-Susceptible Tuberculosis (2016); Interim Guidance: 4-Month Rifapentine-Moxifloxacin Regimen for the Treatment of Drug-Susceptible Pulmonary Tuberculosis - United States, 2022 (2022) [S]</item><item>Infection control and public health: home airborne isolation with no students or visitors and a surgical mask around others; same-day report of suspected tuberculosis to the health department; a contact investigation of his students, friends, and other close contacts led by the health department. Guideline: Official American Thoracic Society/Centers for Disease Control and Prevention/Infectious Diseases Society of America Clinical Practice Guidelines: Treatment of Drug-Susceptible Tuberculosis (2016); Guidelines for the investigation of contacts of persons with infectious tuberculosis: recommendations from the National Tuberculosis Controllers Association and CDC (2005) [S]</item><item>Nutrition: two dietitian visits in the first month, three meals and three energy-dense snacks a day, two oral nutrition supplement drinks a day, and weight at every visit. Guideline: Official American Thoracic Society/Centers for Disease Control and Prevention/Infectious Diseases Society of America Clinical Practice Guidelines: Treatment of Drug-Susceptible Tuberculosis (2016); Consensus statement: Academy of Nutrition and Dietetics and American Society for Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition: characteristics recommended for the identification and documentation of adult malnutrition (undernutrition) (2012) [S]</item><item>Support: plain information about how tuberculosis spreads, how quickly treatment makes him non-infectious, and that it is curable; help with what to tell his students; PHQ-9 at diagnosis, at two months, and at the end of treatment. Guideline: Official American Thoracic Society/Centers for Disease Control and Prevention/Infectious Diseases Society of America Clinical Practice Guidelines: Treatment of Drug-Susceptible Tuberculosis (2016); Depression and Suicide Risk in Adults: Screening (2023) [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
